# Bass swap - what a hand does on the EQ, and the reason a mix sounds clean.
#
# Two kick drums never play at once: the arriving track has no low end until it is most
# of the way in, and the leaving one loses its own at the same moment.

name    Bass swap
note    holds the arriving track's low end back until the swap
align   beat
tempo   free
power   constant

lane out gain
    at 0.0    1.0    power-down
    at 1.0    0.0    hold

lane in gain
    at 0.0    0.0    power-up
    at 1.0    1.0    hold

lane in bass
    at 0.0   -40     smooth
    at 0.5   -40     smooth
    at 0.85    0     hold
    at 1.0     0     hold

lane out bass
    at 0.0     0     smooth
    at 0.5     0     smooth
    at 0.9   -40     hold
    at 1.0   -40     hold
